  {
    "id": "example-cover-control-cover-control-example",
    "type": "comment",
    "name": "Cover control example",
    "info": "A position cover (blind, shutter or curtain motor) owned by the cover controller. Requests go in as \"open\", \"close\", \"stop\", a position from 0 to 100, or a preset name; an automatic target sets respectManual so a person's move holds. The function nodes show the mapping to and from a Zigbee2MQTT cover: wire them to MQTT out and in nodes on your cover's topic. A button can stop the cover if it is moving and open it otherwise, and the cover's availability report keeps requests from going to an offline device. Output 3 says whether the cover is moving, for other policies to react to. Here it pauses motion lighting while the cover moves, through the motion policy's pause input, which never touches the user's own enable.",
    "x": 170,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
